<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dzungar–Qing Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1687–1757</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a>–Qing Wars were a series of conflicts from 1687 to 1757 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and the Dzungar Khanate of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>. Begun by Galdan's attack on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha Mongols</a>, they extended to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and ended with the Qing conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungaria">Dzungaria</a> and the destruction of the Dzungars in the 1750s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dzungar-qing-wars.jpg" alt="Dzungar–Qing Wars" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 钱维城 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pacification_of_the_Dzungars.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
